{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_rating",
      "components": ["T3"],
      "pins": ["T3.1", "T3.2", "T3.3"],
      "nets": ["ATO_VALVE (drain node at H13/P6)", "NET0003", "GND"],
      "observed": "The ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch is implemented with T3 marked 'AO3400A' (a 30 V N-MOSFET), with its drain on the 24 V solenoid node (flyback D3 SS34 to +24V) and gate driven via R3 100R from NET0003 through T7 BT3904.",
      "expected": "Specification §2 states the ATO valve switch is 'T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET)', a 60 V device. Switching a 24 V inductive solenoid load with a 30 V-rated FET leaves almost no margin for transients; a 60 V part is required.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, 'ATO Valve' block (page 3 tile): 'T3 AO3400A' with drain to the 24 V valve node (H13 MC_0.2\", D3 SS34, C43/C21)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch | Netlist: drives ATO_VALVE net; gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The valve-driving MOSFET is rated 30 V instead of the specified 60 V; turn-off transients on the 24 V solenoid can exceed Vds rating, causing premature failure or avalanche stress of the ATO valve switch.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["PR5", "H4"],
      "pins": ["PR5.VCC", "PR5.SDA", "PR5.SCL", "PR5.GND", "H4.1", "H4.2", "H4.3", "H4.4"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0084 (I2C_SDA)", "NET0017 (I2C_SCL)", "GND"],
      "observed": "In the 'Water Height Sensor' block, the LiDAR PR5 is wired through header H4 to the main I2C bus (NET0084/NET0017) and +5V/GND.",
      "expected": "Specification §4.3/§6: the TF-Luna LiDAR 'pins are typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design' and it is marked on_board: no; the intended design leaves it unwired.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, 'WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES' block: 'PR5 LiDAR' VCC/SDA/SCL/GND connected to H4 PB_1.25mm, whose pins carry +5V, NET0084, NET0017, GND"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no ... and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design"}
      ],
      "impact": "A 5 V-powered LiDAR module is connected to the 3.3 V I2C bus; if a module with 5 V pull-ups/levels is plugged in, bus high levels are driven above the ESP32-C6's 3.3 V domain, and the board's behavior deviates from the documented (unwired) design.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic deviates from the intended design in two places: the ATO valve MOSFET is a 30 V AO3400A instead of the specified 60 V AON6407 (insufficient rating for a 24 V inductive load), and the LiDAR that the spec documents as unwired is in fact connected to the I2C bus and +5V. The first finding is the most consequential; the rest of the power train, isolators, TMC2209 drivers and pump switches match the specification's topology."
}

